NOTICE
======

libmc is an independent research project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed
by, or supported by NVIDIA Corporation.

The library uses private NVIDIA RM/UVM interfaces and directly writes GPU
command streams and doorbells. It is experimental software with no warranty.

Third-party sources
-------------------

`third_party/open-gpu-kernel-modules` is an unmodified checkout of NVIDIA's
open GPU kernel modules, pinned at release 610.43.02. Its files retain their
original per-file license terms; see the submodule's `COPYING` file.

The Hopper QMD construction follows the field layout published by Mesa's NVK,
which is MIT licensed. No NVK code is copied; the assignments were written
against the published layout because NVIDIA's Hopper V04 QMD header is not
included in the pinned driver source.

Research provenance
-------------------

The observations, traces, and instrumented driver used to develop libmc live
in https://github.com/maxime-peim/libcuda-research.
